<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30500" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκώμιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώμη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in the village</i>: hence, <i>native, common</i>, 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγχώριος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				344
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶμος</span>) <i>belonging to a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶμος</span>, esp. that which escorted a
			victor in the games: hence, <i>belonging to the praise of a
				conqueror</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. μέλη,
			ὕμνοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				2.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				10.53
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἀμφὶ τρόπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).77
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφάνων ἐγκώμιος τεθμός</span>
			the law <i>of praise</i> for prizes won, ib.<i><span class="en">
				13.29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκώμιον, τό</span>, <i>laudatory ode</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				11.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				13.573f
			</span></i>; generally, <i>eulogy, panegyric</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1205
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.207
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				3.2
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκώμια παλαιῶν ἀνδρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					326a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. εῐς τινα, κατά τινος</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Min.</u>
				319c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				6.9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. λογικόν</span> in prose, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.2727
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Acraephia</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐπικόν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				419
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Oropus</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ
				ἔπαινος τῆς ἀρετῆς</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐ. τῶν ἔργων</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1101b33
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1367b28
			</span></i>.</div>
